    "narrative": "CD-05 (resolves VAL-06, VAL-16, VAL-17) removes three domain-resolution blind spots the validation agents hit in three of six runs. (1) _set_size now expands zero-parameter operator definitions transitively through the EXTENDS hierarchy with a cycle guard -- the same definition map CD-01/F1 resolve_definition_body walks -- and sizes function sets [S -> T] as |T|^|S| consistently with the dimension inference, so tasks \\\\in [Names -> TaskStatus] with TaskStatus defined in an EXTENDS-ed module resolves (was UNKNOWN). (2) Constraints are extracted conjunct-wise via resolve_constraint_chunks (split on /\\\\ and \\\\/, per definition, transitively; chunks never bleed across definition boundaries), so membership conjuncts wrapped across lines resolve (was silent unknown from an end-of-line regex capture). (3) Domain sources merge PER-VARIABLE in the documented order TypeInvariant > TypeOK > configured cfg invariants, first resolvable wins, replacing first-named-definition-wins -- the scaffold multi-view layout resolves both views without renaming tricks; bound_source names every contributing source and each dimension records its source in text and JSON output. F3 preserved: genuinely unresolvable domains stay explicit UNKNOWN (guard test); the resolver coverage contract is documented in references/architecture_tractability.md (What The Domain Resolver Can And Cannot See), which the scanner output now cites. Three regression tests each proven failing pre-fix by stashing the production change (domain_resolution_regressions.txt). Zero TLA+ model delta; all validation green post-reconcile with epic tip 8df525f (CD-04 merged): TLC 283,805 distinct (budget 500,000 with negotiated rationale carried), spec-unit 2 targets (67+64), 583 repo tests, specWorkflow 8/8 and cliWorkflow 2/2 graphs. Deferred: CD-05-DF-01 (pre-existing _set_size literal/union miscount -- silent wrong number shapes needing a depth-aware tokenizer).",
